"""Derive SkyyBazaar/build_skyybazaar_0.1.10.py from the LIVE 0.1.9 (build_skyybazaar_0.1.9.py = the tools/deploy_set.py SET pin, GENERATED by
tools/bazaar_0_1_9_patch.py; 0.1.9 and every older script stay untouched).
Run:  python tools/bazaar_0_1_10_patch.py   then   python SkyyBazaar/build_skyybazaar_0.1.10.py   then   python SkyyBazaar/test_skyybazaar_0.1.10.py

0.1.10 = THE ENCHANTED MATERIALS ARE BAZAAR PRODUCTS (research/Gathering-Shards-Spec.md section 11 phase 1: "Bazaar rows"; research/
Gathering-Progression-Spec.md F14; Skyy 2026-10-06 LOCKED spec Q10 tweak "Enchanted premium" -> "Enchanted items sell a bit ABOVE 100x
base (a premium, capped below any buy -> compress -> sell loop, like the processed-goods 22% rule)"; Skyy 2026-10-03 "if it goes in the
bag, it goes in a matching section in the bizzar.").
 A. 19 NEW PRODUCTS (tools/skyyench.py, the one table; SkyyCollections 0.2.11 ships the items): Enchanted Cobblestone / Rubble / Copper,
    Iron, Thorium, Cobalt, Adamantite Ingots in Mining, the five Enchanted logs in Foraging, the seven Enchanted crops in Farming - the tab
    is SkyySacks 0.8.1's SackDefs.catOf (this build reads max(the SET pin, 0.8.1) of SkyySacks).
 B. PRICE = a PROCESSED GOOD (AUTO): PREMIUM_ITEMS gains ^Skyy_Ench_ ("compressing"), so each is priced from its recipe exactly like the
    bolts: 100 x the RAW value of its input x (1 + the "Processed goods premium" row, default 20 %, max 22 %). The premium is never stacked:
    an Enchanted Iron Ingot is 100 x the iron ingot's RAW value (ore + fuel) x (1 + premium) = 100 Iron Ingots' price, not 100 x 1.2 x 1.2;
    Enchanted Cobblestone = 100 x 1 x 1.2 = 120; Enchanted Rubble = 100 x the cheapest listed rubble x 1.2. One existing row, one existing
    loop proof: the build's loop checks (0.1.2's at premium 0 / 15 / 20 / 22, the 0.1.3 fuel-aware one at EVERY premium 0..22, the SET
    scan) now run over the 19 recipes too and stop the build on any buy -> compress -> sell loop; the Java reprices them like every AUTO
    good (Catalog.reprice0 reads the generated PROC_SPEC). DECISION: no separate Enchanted premium row (Skyy's lock names the processed
    22 % rule; the Gathering-Shards draft's 10 % idea would need a second capped row for the same loop bound).
 C. THE ONE-TIME UPDATE (PROJECT-RULES 4, the migrate19 pattern, copied): Catalog.migrate110 runs once after migrate19 (marker
    migrated.0.1.10 in pricing.properties, kept by writeModes): a verified byte copy of products.properties to config-history/ first, then
    each of the 19 ids not in the file yet is APPENDED as its seed line (every existing byte / line ending kept); one trades.log line per
    product with its undo + a summary line; one INFO line. A failed step writes no marker and retries at the next start. A fresh install
    is seeded with every product.
No other price, product, tab or trade changes. Rolling back to 0.1.9: safe - the appended lines are ordinary product lines (0.1.9 trades
them as fixed-price products in their file category; it cannot price them from a recipe it does not know).
Classes changed: Catalog (+ NEW0110 / MIGRATED110 / M110_LOG / migrate110; loadModes, writeModes; the generated seed / PROC tables in
<clinit>), SkyyBazaarPlugin.setup (migrate110 + its log lines), CfgFn / CfgRows (version text).
"""
